@startuml
title Figure 4a-2  Activity Diagram — Fieldwork Execution and Feedback Loops\n[Individual task · Member B]\nPer-procedure execution inside an A6 instance (engine split, validation, A7, Loop 1, auto-disposition, safe point) is Figure 4b (Member C)

skinparam defaultFontSize 20
skinparam legendFontSize 20
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #444444
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #888800
skinparam ConditionEndStyle diamond

|Human|
|Concierge|
|Orchestrator & Rule Engine|
|LLM Agent|

|Orchestrator & Rule Engine|
(P)
note right
  from Figure 4a-1 (Member A):
  plan vN approved, execution bound to vN
end note
fork
  |Concierge|
  while (P2 not settled: ReviewQueue publishes tasks?) is (yes)
    :Present next ReviewTask by 9.1 tier with the decisions
    allowed for its kind: reasoning chain, evidence,
    counter-argument, A7 verdict (blind: conclusion hidden,
    dispute: A6 and A7 side by side no ranking,
    failed / unattributed: rule result or failure reason,
    scope_limited: request);
    |Human|
    :Decide within the allowed set: confirm / override
    with conclusion / misstatement / more procedures /
    adjudicate / approve scope_limited / rerun /
    manual result / not applicable / evidence unreliable;
    |Concierge|
    :Build ReviewRecord (taskId, targetVersion, decision,
    structured payload, reason, empty reason rejected),
    submit(ReviewRecord) via DecisionSubmit, log dwell time;
    |Orchestrator & Rule Engine|
    if (Target version current, gate state valid\nand decision allowed for task kind?) then (no)
      :Reject submission, re-present
      latest version with allowed decisions;
    else (yes)
      switch (Decision?)
      case (confirm / override / misstatement)
        :reviewStatus confirmed, or
        overrideConclusion = new Judgment
        version (old -> supersededBy), or
        Misstatement created from
        misstatementDraft (handled in P3);
      case (more procedures)
        :Loop 2: requestedProcedures
        added to pack (A5 evidence task
        or substantive procedures),
        Procedure -> executing,
        trigger loop2_extend;
      case (adjudicate)
        :Write disputeResolution:
        a6_upheld -> keep A6 conclusion,
        a7_upheld -> A7 conclusion = new version,
        neither -> neitherAction: human
        conclusion or more procedures,
        consulted flag + record if consulted;
      case (scope_limited)
        :management_imposed: GEN-19 record
        of removal request required first,
        else reject, write six fields
        (Aus 23.1), Procedure -> scope_limited;
      case (rerun / manual result / not applicable / evidence unreliable)
        :rerun: Procedure -> executing,
        trigger rerun with rerunParams,
        manual result: manualResult
        becomes the Judgment,
        not applicable: Procedure ->
        not_applicable with reason,
        evidence unreliable: dependent
        Judgments -> stale (propagation);
      endswitch
      :Recompute Procedure status: completed only when every
      ReviewTask of the procedure is decided, no open dispute,
      no follow-up run pending and the period is covered
      (timing != interim or periodCovered), otherwise it stays
      awaiting_human / in_dispute, moves to executing, or
      parks in interim_completed until its GEN-24 completes;
      if (Misstatement or risk data changed\nand Loop 3 blocking condition hit?) then (yes)
        :Raise reassessment flag,
        non-compliance or undue influence:
        GEN-13 NoclarMatter + GEN-14
        StatutoryReport clock (M-12);
      else (no)
      endif
    endif
    |Concierge|
  endwhile (pack settled)
  detach
fork again
  |Orchestrator & Rule Engine|
  :A5 sends confirmation requests once at layer 0
  (CSH-04, REC-05), registers reminder_days and
  deadline_days timers, returns immediately;
  while (Confirmation event during P2?\nreply received (A3 DOC-06), reminder timer, deadline timer) is (yes)
    switch (Event?)
    case (reminder, no reply)
      :A5 second request
      (idempotent key);
    case (reply received)
      :Record Confirmation result,
      release dependent procedures
      CSH-02 / REC-03 to schedule
      (agree -> pass, difference ->
      Judgment via Figure 4b);
    case (deadline, no reply)
      :Release alternative procedures
      REC-02 to schedule (subsequent
      receipts, contracts, shipping docs),
      none obtainable -> ReviewTask
      scope_limited;
    endswitch
  endwhile (P2 ends)
  detach
fork again
  |Orchestrator & Rule Engine|
  :P2 starts at layer 0;
end merge
repeat
  |Orchestrator & Rule Engine|
  :Schedule current layer: build DAG, topological
  layers, group by cycle (cap 4), deterministic table,
  procedures waiting for a confirmation event stay planned,
  GEN-24 becomes ready when its interim procedure is
  interim_completed, no dispatch while reassessment flag is raised;
  fork
    :A6 instance fw-L-0: for each procedure
    in subset run Figure 4b until subset
    done or reassessment flag raised;
  fork again
    :A6 instances fw-L-1 .. fw-L-k: same on
    own subset, remainder of a failed
    instance re-assigned;
  end fork
  :Fan-in: merge StatePatches by ID into EngagementState
  and AuditOutputStore (reducer keeps highest version),
  ReviewTask drafts from the instances are published
  to the queue here after validation,
  auto-closed results do not enter the queue;

  if (Reassessment flag raised?) then (yes)
    :Instances stopped at safe points,
    completed Judgments kept;
    |LLM Agent|
    :A4 re-reasons on new evidence and rule summary:
    risk change proposal, affected procedures;
    repeat
      |Concierge|
      :Present risk change proposal (GATE-R);
      |Human|
      :Approve or reject with reason;
      |Concierge|
      :Build GateDecision, submit via DecisionSubmit;
      |Orchestrator & Rule Engine|
      :Validate target version and gate state;
    backward :Re-present latest version;
    repeat while (Valid?) is (no) not (yes)
    switch (GATE-R decision?)
    case (approve)
      :RiskItem version +1 (reason, time, approver),
      mark affected completed procedures needs_review,
      fraud trigger: GEN-16 discussion with governance first,
      clear flag, re-assemble pack without data re-ingest;
      (R)
      note right
        back to pack assembly in Figure 4a-1 (Member A)
      end note
      detach
    case (reject)
      :Record reason, clear flag,
      resume from paused position (history state);
    case (withdraw)
      :ACC-10: record decision, seal workpapers
      (hashes, read-only), Engagement -> Withdrawn,
      statutory clocks keep running;
      stop
    endswitch
  else (no)
  endif

  |Orchestrator & Rule Engine|
  :Published ReviewTasks are handled by the review lane
  in parallel (fork above), the layer loop does not wait
  for human decisions;
repeat while (Pack settled?\nall procedures completed / not_applicable / scope_limited,\nno open dispute, no confirmation pending,\nno pending layer, no reassessment flag) is (no) not (yes)
:To P3 Completion (FIN-05 completeness check);
stop

legend right
  |= Lane |= Who |
  | Human | RCA; exchanges messages only with Concierge |
  | Concierge | A10; presents ReviewTasks, assigns manual tasks, collects decisions verbatim (form fallback: same fields) |
  | Orchestrator & Rule Engine | A1 (scheduling, validation, persistence, events), A5 EvidenceAgent, RuleEngine; deterministic, no LLM |
  | LLM Agent | A4 RiskAssessor, A6 FieldworkAgent, A7 ReviewAgent |
  |= Decision path |= |
  | All human decisions | A10 builds GateDecision / ReviewRecord -> DecisionSubmit -> A1 validates target version and gate state -> writes |
  |= Loop |= Level |
  | Loop 1 | Procedure level, inside A6 instance, Figure 4b |
  | Loop 2 | Cycle level, human-initiated additional procedures |
  | Loop 3 | Engagement level, flag at safe point, GATE-R approve / reject / withdraw, plan version +1 |
  |= Withdrawal |= |
  | ACC-10 | Any phase (Figure 3a): GateDecision.disposition = withdraw, workpapers sealed |
  |= Confirmation |= |
  | Asynchronous | A5 sends once and returns; replies and timers are events; only dependent procedures wait, fan-in and GATE-R do not |
  |= Review lane |= |
  | Parallel | The ReviewTask lane runs as its own branch of the P2 fork; layer scheduling never waits for a human decision, the two lanes meet only at the pack settled condition |
endlegend
@enduml
